    <DataNode elementId="AT1G03630-MONOMER" textLabel="Protochlorophyllide reductase C, chloroplastic" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O48741" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="335" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">A cDNA encoding for a novel NADPH-protochlorophyllide oxidoreductase (POR C) has been identified in &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;. The POR C protein was expressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; and its molecular function confirmed. In contrast to POR B which is under the control of the circadian clock POR C expression remained unaffected by the light/dark shift. The three known POR&apos;s act differentially under a given light regime and are therefore discussed as adaptive enzymes to the plants light conditions |CITS: [SU01]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G03630-MONOMER" />
